{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070981-gnosis-reduction-from-creating-soul-stones","id":1070981,"title":"Gnosis Reduction from creating Soul Stones","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-03-30T19:01:34-07:00","id":1070981,"title":"Gnosis Reduction from creating Soul Stones","content":"What happens when you create enough Soul Stones that your maximum Gnosis is less than your current Gnosis? Is it impossible, or does it decrease your Gnosis? If so, is it a permanent decrease, or do you get it back when Soul Stone is destroyed? What happens if the Gnosis reduction makes your Maximum Arcana limit less than your current biggest Arcanum? Do you unlearn them? What happens to your Legacy Attainments? Do you unlearn them, or just suppress them until your Gnosis is back? What happens if your Gnosis drops to 0 this way?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-30T19:11:55-07:00","id":1070987,"title":"","content":"I assume that you can't.<br /> <br /> If it could happen though then you'd suffer a permanent decrease until the soul stones are destroyed and you'd lose your maximum arcana ratings, attainments require Gnosis to function so you'd lose those too. I doubt you'd unlearn anything though, I certainly wouldn't expect my players to pay the XP again.<br /> <br /> If you drop to Gnosis 0 you've become a Sleepwalker, you might be viable as a Proximi, kind of an ST call there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-30T20:45:13-07:00","id":1071013,"title":"","content":"This is how I would do it. I would say that your gnosis allows you to figure out certain things and then acquire the power that comes with them, but <i>after </i>that your gnosis is just the raw horse-power of your awakened will. You don't need it for higher magic, but you'll be sorely hurting otherwise.<br /> <br /> I would have soul stones reduce your gnosis if you make too many of them, but you keep all powers not <i>directly</i> tied to gnosis. The powers that <i>do </i>decrease, I would say, would be:<br /> How fast you spend Mana.<br /> How much mana you can hold.<br /> Your yantra slots.<br /> Your spell control.<br /> How quickly you can perform rituals.<br /> And it <i>might</i> affect paradox rolls. I would say <i>no</i> just because I think paradox is too easy to avoid anyway? But since Changelings can try and decrease their wyrd to mitigate drawbacks they can no longer deal with, I can see ST's and players wanting a Mage to do that too--so it would be up to your ST or you. Perhaps making the soul stones could be used to help control your paradox chance.<br /> <br /> So you could have, possibly, a 4th degree Master who has 9 soul-stones and 1 gnosis. This master is capable of a wiiiide range of potent magic, but none of their spells are particularly strong because they lack the gnosis to feed an effective dice pool and their rituals take <i>foreeeveeeer.</i> If the paradox reduction was considered a fair trade off, it is also because this person now has 9 soul stones to protect... and that's <i>really</i> dangerous. Someone destroys all of those at once and you <i>will</i> die.... or they could force you to perform 27 favors for them!<br /> <br /> I hope those ideas will help you or your fellows find a good way to deal with this.<br /> <br /> And I agree with mrmdubois that gnosis 0 makes you a sleepwalker. Probably not a proximus though unless you were a proximus when you awoke...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}